<Base title="Website Privacy Policy" counterpart="/zh/privacy-policy/" description="How Reminiscence Cloud handles information associated with this website."><article class="legal-page"><p class="kicker">Privacy</p><h1>Website Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lede">How Reminiscence Cloud handles information associated with this website.</p><p class="legal-meta"><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> September 20, 2026</p><aside class="legal-alert"><strong>Website policy—not a clinical privacy notice.</strong> This policy covers the public website. Clinical records and protected health information are addressed separately in the <a href="/hipaa-notice/">HIPAA Notice of Privacy Practices</a> and the practice’s intake documents.</aside><h2>Information this website handles</h2><p>This is a static informational website. It does not currently contain an intake form, patient portal, payment system, analytics service, advertising tracker, or marketing cookie. Routine technical information—such as an IP address, browser type, requested page, date and time, and security events—may be processed automatically by the website host and internet infrastructure needed to deliver and protect the site.</p><p>The site itself does not set optional advertising or personalization cookies. If this changes, this policy should be revised before the new technology is enabled.</p><h2>Consultation and clinical communications</h2><p>The consultation pages preserve the practice’s public booking addresses but do not yet collect information. Before launch, they must be connected to a practice-approved secure scheduling or inquiry service. That service will have its own privacy terms and data practices.</p><p>Please do not send sensitive clinical information through ordinary email, social media, or a general website form. These channels may not be appropriate for confidential or urgent communications. Established clients should use the communication methods provided by the practice.</p><h2>How information may be used</h2><p>Technical information processed to deliver the site may be used for security, troubleshooting, reliability, and aggregate site administration. Information voluntarily submitted through an approved consultation service may be used to respond to the inquiry, assess service availability and fit, arrange a consultation, maintain appropriate business records, and comply with legal obligations.</p><h2>Service providers and external links</h2><p>Hosting, domain, security, scheduling, and image-delivery providers may process limited technical information on behalf of the practice under their own terms. Pages containing Pexels photographs request those image files from images.pexels.com; Pexels may receive the visitor’s IP address, browser information, and request details needed to deliver them. Links to Instagram, LinkedIn, or another external service take you to a third-party website. Reminiscence Cloud does not control those sites or their privacy practices; review their policies before providing information.</p><h2>Data retention and security</h2><p>Information should be retained only as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected and to meet applicable professional, contractual, and legal obligations. Reasonable safeguards are used, but no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p><h2>Your choices and questions</h2><p>You may avoid providing personal information through this website. Questions, access requests, or correction requests should be directed to the practice through its approved contact method. The practice’s public privacy contact information must be added before launch.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>This website is intended to provide information about adult psychotherapy services and is not directed to children under 13. The site does not knowingly solicit personal information from children.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>This policy may be updated when the website’s technology, vendors, services, or legal obligations change. The revised version and review date will be posted on this page.</p></article></Base>
